Elena Jane Goulding ( [LINK: (/ˈɡoʊldɪŋ/) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:IPA/English]   [LINK: (GOHL-ding) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Pronunciation_respelling_key] ; born 30 December 1986) is an English  [LINK: (singer-songwriter) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Singer-songwriter] . Born in  [LINK: (Hereford) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hereford]  and raised in  [LINK: (Lyonshall) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lyonshall] , Goulding began writing songs at the age of 15. She released her debut single " [LINK: (Under the Sheets) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Under_the_Sheets] " through  [LINK: (Neon Gold Records) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neon_Gold_Records]  in 2009, and signed with  [LINK: (Polydor Records) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polydor_Records]  that same year, releasing her debut  [LINK: (extended play) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Extended_play]  (EP)  [LINK: (An Introduction to Ellie Goulding) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/An_Introduction_to_Ellie_Goulding] . [LINK: ([1]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-1]  Her debut studio album,  [LINK: (Lights) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lights_(Ellie_Goulding_album)]  (2010), debuted at No. 1 on the  [LINK: (UK Albums Chart) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/UK_Albums_Chart] , and was reissued as Bright Lights, spawning three successful singles: a cover of  [LINK: (Elton John) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elton_John] 's " [LINK: (Your Song) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Your_Song_(Ellie_Goulding_song)] ", " [LINK: (Starry Eyed) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Starry_Eyed_(Ellie_Goulding_song)] " and " [LINK: (Lights) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lights_(Ellie_Goulding_song)] ".

Goulding's second studio album,  [LINK: (Halcyon) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Halcyon_(album)]  (2012), was preceded by its lead single " [LINK: (Anything Could Happen) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anything_Could_Happen] ", and a repackaged edition titled  [LINK: (Halcyon Days) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Halcyon_Days_(Ellie_Goulding_album)]  (2013) produced the single " [LINK: (Burn) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burn_(Ellie_Goulding_song)] ", which became her first No. 1 single in the UK. She then collaborated with DJ  [LINK: (Calvin Harris) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calvin_Harris]  on two singles: " [LINK: (I Need Your Love) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/I_Need_Your_Love_(Calvin_Harris_song)] " and " [LINK: (Outside) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Outside_(Calvin_Harris_song)] ". After the release of her third studio album  [LINK: (Delirium) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Delirium_(Ellie_Goulding_album)]  (2015) and its lead single " [LINK: (On My Mind) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/On_My_Mind_(Ellie_Goulding_song)] ", Goulding received a  [LINK: (Grammy Award) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grammy_Award]  nomination for her single " [LINK: (Love Me Like You Do) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Love_Me_Like_You_Do] ", which was recorded for the  [LINK: (soundtrack) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fifty_Shades_of_Grey_(soundtrack)]  of  [LINK: (Fifty Shades of Grey) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fifty_Shades_of_Grey_(film)]  (2015). [LINK: ([2]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-58Grammys-2]

Goulding took a hiatus from 2016 to 2020, struggling with an  [LINK: (anxiety disorder) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anxiety_disorder]  and media scrutiny over false claims about her personal life. [LINK: ([3]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-3]  [LINK: ([4]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-4]  Her fourth studio album  [LINK: (Brightest Blue) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brightest_Blue]  (2020) became her third album to top the UK Albums Chart, and her fourth consecutive album certified by the  [LINK: (Recording Industry Association of America) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Recording_Industry_Association_of_America]  (RIAA). It spawned several singles, including the hits " [LINK: (Close to Me) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Close_to_Me_(Ellie_Goulding,_Diplo_and_Swae_Lee_song)] ", " [LINK: (Hate Me) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hate_Me_(Ellie_Goulding_and_Juice_Wrld_song)] " and " [LINK: (Sixteen) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sixteen_(Ellie_Goulding_song)] ". [LINK: ([5]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-5]  She reunited with Harris on the single " [LINK: (Miracle) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Miracle_(Calvin_Harris_and_Ellie_Goulding_song)] ", which spent eight non-consecutive weeks at No. 1 on the  [LINK: (UK Singles Chart) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/UK_Singles_Chart]  in 2023. [LINK: ([6]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-6]  Goulding's fifth studio album  [LINK: (Higher Than Heaven) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Higher_Than_Heaven]  (2023) debuted at No. 1 in the UK, her fourth chart-topping album, making her the British female with the most number-one albums in UK history, tying with  [LINK: (Adele) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adele] . [LINK: ([7]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-7]  [LINK: ([8]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-8]

Goulding is the recipient of numerous  [LINK: (accolades) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_awards_and_nominations_received_by_Ellie_Goulding] , including two  [LINK: (Brit Awards) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brit_Awards] , a  [LINK: (Brit Billion Award) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brits_Billion_Award] , a  [LINK: (Billboard Music Award) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Billboard_Music_Awards] , 17  [LINK: (BMI London Awards) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BMI_Film_%26_TV_Awards] , and two  [LINK: (Grammy) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grammy_Awards]  nominations. [LINK: ([9]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-Variety_awards-9]  She was honoured with a Decade Award by the  [LINK: (Variety Hitmakers Awards) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Variety_Hitmakers_Awards]  in recognition of a decade of "undeniable hits" and  [LINK: (TIME100) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Time_100]  honoured her with the  [LINK: (Impact Award) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Time100_Impact_Awards]  for using her platform to protect the environment. [LINK: ([9]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-Variety_awards-9]  [LINK: ([10]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-10]  [LINK: ([11]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-11]  She has sold more than 27 million albums and 216 million singles, and amassed 43 billion streams worldwide, [LINK: ([12]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-12]  making her one of the most successful British female singers of the 21st century. [LINK: ([13]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-13]  [LINK: ([14]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-14]


# EARLY LIFE #

Elena Jane Goulding was born on 30 December 1986 [LINK: ([15]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-15]  in  [LINK: (Hereford) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hereford] ,  [LINK: (Herefordshire) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Herefordshire] , England, to Arthur and Tracey Goulding, and was brought up in the small village of  [LINK: (Lyonshall) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lyonshall] , in Herefordshire. She has a brother, Alex, and two sisters, Isabel and Jordan. When she was five years old, her parents separated. [LINK: ([16]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-16]  Afterwards, she had little contact with her father, a funeral director. [LINK: ([17]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-IndependentMeToo-17]  Goulding and her siblings were raised by their mother on a  [LINK: (council estate) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Council_estate] , [LINK: ([18]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-18]  with Goulding describing the family as "super poor". [LINK: ([19]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-19]  Goulding has stated that she has a "difficult" relationship with her mother. [LINK: ([17]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-IndependentMeToo-17]

Goulding began playing the  [LINK: (clarinet) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clarinet]  at age nine and began learning guitar when she was 14. She attended  [LINK: (Lady Hawkins' High School) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lady_Hawkins%27_High_School]  in  [LINK: (Kington, Herefordshire) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kington,_Herefordshire]  and, by the age of 15, started writing songs. She took  [LINK: (A levels) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GCE_Advanced_Level]  in English, politics, drama and music, and passed three with "A" grades but failed music. [LINK: ([20]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-20]  [LINK: ([21]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-21]  She enrolled on a degree in Drama and Theatre Studies at the  [LINK: (University of Kent) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/University_of_Kent] , but did not complete her studies, quitting in her final year. [LINK: ([22]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-22]  After meeting Jamie Lillywhite, he became her manager and introduced her to the producer  [LINK: (Starsmith) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Starsmith] , who would become her chief collaborator and the primary producer of Lights. [LINK: ([23]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-23]


# CAREER #

Although Ellie Goulding signed to  [LINK: (Polydor Records) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polydor_Records]  in July 2009, her debut single, " [LINK: (Under the Sheets) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Under_the_Sheets] ", was released through the independent label  [LINK: (Neon Gold Records) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neon_Gold_Records] , appearing  [LINK: (digitally) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_download]  in the United Kingdom on 15 November 2009. [LINK: ([24]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-hitquarters-24]  [LINK: ([25]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-HerTim-25]  [LINK: ([26]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-26]  The single peaked at No. 53 on the  [LINK: (UK Singles Chart) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/UK_Singles_Chart]  following Goulding's appearance on  [LINK: (Later... with Jools Holland) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Later..._with_Jools_Holland]  (performing "Under the Sheets" and " [LINK: (Guns and Horses) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guns_and_Horses] ") [LINK: ([27]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-27]  and a UK tour supporting  [LINK: (Little Boots) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Little_Boots] . [LINK: ([28]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-28]  [LINK: ([29]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-UK_chart-29]  "Wish I Stayed" was available as a free download as Single of the Week on  [LINK: (iTunes Store) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ITunes_Store]  UK from 22 to 28 December 2009. [LINK: ([30]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-30]

Before the release of her debut album, Goulding won the  [LINK: (BBC Sound of 2010) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sound_of...]  poll, which showcases the music industry's top choices for rising stars. [LINK: ([31]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-31]  She also won the Critics' Choice Award at the  [LINK: (2010 Brit Awards) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2010_Brit_Awards] , making her the second artist to win both in the same year. [LINK: ([32]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-32]  Goulding co-wrote "Love Me 'Cause You Want To" for  [LINK: (Gabriella Cilmi) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gabriella_Cilmi] 's second album,  [LINK: (Ten) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ten_(Gabriella_Cilmi_album)] , and three songs ("Remake Me + You", "Notice", "Jumping into Rivers") for  [LINK: (Diana Vickers) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diana_Vickers] 's debut album,  [LINK: (Songs from the Tainted Cherry Tree) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Songs_from_the_Tainted_Cherry_Tree] . [LINK: ([33]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-33]  Her song "Not Following" was used by German singer  [LINK: (Lena) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lena_Meyer-Landrut]  on her debut album  [LINK: (My Cassette Player) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/My_Cassette_Player] . [LINK: ([34]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-34]  Goulding was featured on rapper  [LINK: (Tinie Tempah) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tinie_Tempah] 's single " [LINK: (Wonderman) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wonderman_(Tinie_Tempah_song)] " from his debut studio album  [LINK: (Disc-Overy) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Disc-Overy]  (2010).

Goulding's debut album  [LINK: (Lights) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lights_(Ellie_Goulding_album)]  was released in March 2010, reaching No. 1 on the  [LINK: (UK Albums Chart) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/UK_Albums_Chart]  and No. 6 on the  [LINK: (Irish Albums Chart) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Irish_Albums_Chart] . [LINK: ([35]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-35]  [LINK: ([36]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-36]  [LINK: ([37]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-37]  Its singles " [LINK: (Starry Eyed) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Starry_Eyed_(Ellie_Goulding_song)] ", " [LINK: (Guns and Horses) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guns_and_Horses] ", and " [LINK: (The Writer) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Writer_(song)] " peaked at Nos. 4, 26, and 19. [LINK: ([29]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-UK_chart-29]  As of June 2012, the album had sold over 850,000 copies in the UK and 1.6 million copies worldwide. [LINK: ([38]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-38]  In August 2010, she released a second EP,  [LINK: (Run into the Light) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Run_into_the_Light] , containing remixes of songs from Lights. The album was supported by  [LINK: (Nike) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nike,_Inc.]  and was released through Polydor as a running soundtrack in an effort to get her music taken up by the running subculture. [LINK: ([39]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-Running-39]  In November 2010, Lights was re-released as Bright Lights, with six new tracks added. It was originally announced that the lead single from Bright Lights would be the new edit of the  [LINK: (title track) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lights_(Ellie_Goulding_song)]  with a release scheduled for 1 November 2010. [LINK: ([40]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-40]  This plan was ultimately scrapped to allow her cover of  [LINK: (Elton John) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elton_John] 's " [LINK: (Your Song) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Your_Song_(Ellie_Goulding_song)] " to be released in conjunction with the  [LINK: (John Lewis Christmas advert) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Lewis_Christmas_advert]  in the UK in 2010. The single became her second highest-charting single to date, reaching No. 2 on the UK Singles Chart. [LINK: ([29]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-UK_chart-29]  It also charted in some European countries. [LINK: ([41]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-41]  In January 2011, it was announced that the title track from Lights would serve as the second single from Bright Lights. [LINK: ([42]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-42]  "Lights" reached No. 49 on the UK Singles Chart, [LINK: ([29]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-UK_chart-29]  while becoming Goulding's first song to chart in the United States, as well as her highest-charting song to date, peaking at No. 2 on the  [LINK: (Billboard Hot 100) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Billboard_Hot_100]  in August 2012. [LINK: ([43]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-43]

Goulding toured in support of Lights and supported  [LINK: (Passion Pit) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Passion_Pit]  in March 2010 and  [LINK: (John Mayer) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Mayer]  [LINK: ([44]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-44]  during his British tour in May 2010. [LINK: ([45]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-45]  During the summer she performed at a number of festivals. On 29 May she performed at the  [LINK: (Dot to Dot Festival) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dot_to_Dot_Festival]  in Bristol. [LINK: ([46]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-autogenerated1-46]  She performed a set on 25 June at the  [LINK: (Glastonbury Festival 2010) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glastonbury_Festival_2010]  on the John Peel Stage. [LINK: ([47]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-47]  Her third EP was a live recording of part of her set at the  [LINK: (iTunes Festival) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ITunes_Festival]  2010. [LINK: ([48]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-48]  The whole set was ultimately included as bonus content on the iTunes version of Bright Lights. [LINK: ([49]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-49]  She made her  [LINK: (T in the Park) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/T_in_the_Park_2010]  debut on 11 July. [LINK: ([50]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-50]  In early 2011, she recorded an original song for the film  [LINK: (Life in a Day) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Life_in_a_Day_(2011_film)] . Ellie Goulding was No. 5 on  [LINK: (Rolling Stone) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rolling_Stone] 's annual hot list in February 2011. [LINK: ([51]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-51]  In February 2011, she returned to the  [LINK: (Brit Awards) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2011_Brit_Awards]  where she was nominated for Best British Female and Best British Breakthrough Act but lost out to  [LINK: (Laura Marling) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laura_Marling]  and to  [LINK: (Tinie Tempah) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tinie_Tempah] . [LINK: ([52]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-52]

In April 2011, Goulding played live at the  [LINK: (Coachella Valley Music and Arts Festival) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coachella_Valley_Music_and_Arts_Festival] . [LINK: ([53]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-TelegraphObsessed-53]  She also made her American television debut on  [LINK: (Jimmy Kimmel Live!) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jimmy_Kimmel_Live!]  on 7 April 2011 performing "Starry Eyed". She appeared as the musical guest on the 700th episode of the  [LINK: (Saturday Night Live) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saturday_Night_Live] , broadcast 7 May 2011 and hosted by  [LINK: (Tina Fey) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tina_Fey] . [LINK: ([54]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-54]  [LINK: ([55]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-55]  She performed at the wedding reception of  [LINK: (Prince William and Kate Middleton) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wedding_of_Prince_William_and_Catherine_Middleton]  on 29 April 2011, [LINK: ([56]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-56]  and performed what she recalled as "about 14 songs", including her cover of "Your Song". [LINK: ([57]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-billboard-may2011-57]

Goulding collaborated with American electronic artist and producer  [LINK: (Skrillex) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skrillex]  on a song titled "Summit", included on his 2011 EP  [LINK: (Bangarang) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bangarang_(EP)] . She travelled with Skrillex on his South American tour [LINK: ([58]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-58] 
She headlined the 2011  [LINK: (Wakestock Festival) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wakestock_(Wales)]  in Wales, performing on 8 July. [LINK: ([59]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-59]  In August, she performed at the  [LINK: (V Festival) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/V_Festival#V2011]  for her second year in a row. [LINK: ([60]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-60]  Following the re-release of Lights and the American release of the album, Goulding said she would soon begin work on a second studio album with an expected release of September 2011. [LINK: ([61]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-61]  On 6 August 2011, she performed at  [LINK: (Lollapalooza) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lollapalooza]  in Chicago. [LINK: ([62]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-62]  She performed at the annual  [LINK: (Nobel Peace Prize Concert) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nobel_Peace_Prize_Concert]  on 11 December 2011 in  [LINK: (Oslo) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oslo] , Norway. On 1 December 2011, she performed at the  [LINK: (White House) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White_House]  during the  [LINK: (National Christmas Tree) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Christmas_Tree_(United_States)]  lighting, alongside  [LINK: (Big Time Rush) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Big_Time_Rush_(TV_series)]  and  [LINK: (will.i.am) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Will.i.am] . [LINK: ([63]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-63]  On 19 September 2011, it was announced that she would open for  [LINK: (Katy Perry) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Katy_Perry] 's  [LINK: (California Dreams Tour) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/California_Dreams_Tour] , replacing  [LINK: (Jessie J) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jessie_J]  who withdrew due to a foot injury. [LINK: ([64]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-64]  [LINK: ([65]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-65]

In 2012, Goulding appeared on "Fall into the Sky" from  [LINK: (Zedd) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zedd_(producer)] 's debut album  [LINK: (Clarity) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clarity_(Zedd_album)]  and on  [LINK: (Calvin Harris) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calvin_Harris] 's song " [LINK: (I Need Your Love) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/I_Need_Your_Love_(Calvin_Harris_song)] " which is included on Halcyon and also Harris's album  [LINK: (18 Months) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/18_Months] . On 10 July 2012, Goulding released a cover of  [LINK: (Active Child) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Active_Child] 's song "Hanging On", featuring Tinie Tempah, as a free download on her  [LINK: (SoundCloud) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SoundCloud]  page. [LINK: ([66]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-66]  In late July 2012, it was announced that Goulding's second album is titled  [LINK: (Halcyon) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Halcyon_(album)]  and it would be released on 8 October 2012. The album was preceded by the lead single " [LINK: (Anything Could Happen) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anything_Could_Happen] " on 21 August. [LINK: ([67]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-67]  The lyric video for "Anything Could Happen" premiered on 9 August 2012, consisting of a series of fan-submitted  [LINK: (Instagram) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Instagram]  pictures. [LINK: ([68]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-68] 
On 19 November 2012, the music video for Goulding's second single from Halcyon, titled " [LINK: (Figure 8) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Figure_8_(song)] " was released. The single was released digitally in the UK on 12 December 2012. The song charted before it was released, and made its way into the top 40 in the UK, peaking at No. 33.

Goulding contributed a track titled "Bittersweet" (produced by  [LINK: (Skrillex) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skrillex] ) to the soundtrack of  [LINK: (The Twilight Saga: Breaking Dawn – Part 2) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Twilight_Saga:_Breaking_Dawn_%E2%80%93_Part_2_(soundtrack)] , released on 13 November 2012. [LINK: ([69]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-69]  It was announced on 12 February 2013, that in May 2013, she would be supporting  [LINK: (Bruno Mars) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bruno_Mars]  on his Moonshine Jungle World Tour on selected dates. [LINK: ([70]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-70]  On 20 May 2013, Goulding announced she would embark on a seven-date tour in the UK during October that year. [LINK: ([71]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-71]  On 28 May 2013, Goulding's cover of  [LINK: (Alt-J) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alt-J] 's song " [LINK: (Tessellate) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tessellate_(song)] " was released via her SoundCloud page. [LINK: ([72]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-72]  Goulding has also been reported to have filmed a music video for this track in Paris earlier that month. She claimed to be "making a video for a song that isn't on my record". [LINK: ([73]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-73] 
In June 2013, Goulding performed at previous festivals and concerts including  [LINK: (RockNess) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/RockNess]  festival in  [LINK: (Inverness) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inverness] , Capital FM Summertime Ball and  [LINK: (Firefly Music Festival) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Firefly_Music_Festival]  at The Woodlands in  [LINK: (Dover, Delaware) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dover,_Delaware] . On 2 July 2013, Goulding premiered a song titled "You My Everything" in the first episode of  [LINK: (Skins Fire) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skins_(UK_TV_series)]  [LINK: ([74]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-74]  and that same day Goulding confirmed to  [LINK: (Elle) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elle_(magazine)]  magazine that Halcyon would be re-released later that year. [LINK: ([75]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-75]

On 5 July 2013, Digital Spy confirmed the release of  [LINK: (Halcyon Days) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Halcyon_Days_(Ellie_Goulding_album)] , a repackaged edition of Halcyon, which was released on 23 August 2013. [LINK: ([76]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-76]  The re-release, featuring ten additional tracks, was preceded by the single " [LINK: (Burn) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burn_(Ellie_Goulding_song)] ", which had been uploaded to Goulding's  [LINK: (SoundCloud) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SoundCloud]  page the previous day. [LINK: ([77]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-77]  [LINK: ([78]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-78]  On 7 July 2013, the official music video for "Burn" premiered on Goulding's Vevo channel on  [LINK: (YouTube) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/YouTube] . "Burn" became Goulding's first single to top the UK's Official Singles Chart. [LINK: ([79]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-79] 
Goulding was performing at V Festival Chelmsford when news of her first UK No. 1 broke;  [LINK: (Rita Ora) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rita_Ora]  surprised Goulding with her Official Number 1 Award. [LINK: ([80]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-80]  On 9 September 2013, Goulding released a music video for " [LINK: (How Long Will I Love You) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/How_Long_Will_I_Love_You%3F#Ellie_Goulding_version] " for the film  [LINK: (About Time) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/About_Time_(2013_film)] . [LINK: ([81]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-81]  Goulding appeared on the soundtrack for the film  [LINK: (The Hunger Games: Catching Fire) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Hunger_Games:_Catching_Fire]  with the track "Mirror".

On 15 October 2013, Goulding confirmed on  [LINK: (Fearne Cotton) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fearne_Cotton] 's radio show that "How Long Will I Love You" would be the next single for BBC's Children in Need. [LINK: ([82]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-82]  On the same day, the  [LINK: (Active Child) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Active_Child]  song "Silhouette", on which Goulding features, was also released. [LINK: ([83]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-83]  On 28 October 2013, Goulding posted an alternative video of "How Long Will I Love You" on her Vevo channel for the short film Tom & Issy, in which she also stars. [LINK: ([84]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-entertainmentwise.com-84]  On the final episode of  [LINK: (The X Factor) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_X_Factor_(UK_series_10)]  on 14 December, Goulding performed a duet with finalist  [LINK: (Luke Friend) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Luke_Friend] . [LINK: ([85]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-85]

On 5 January 2014, Goulding premiered the music video for her song "Goodness Gracious" on her Vevo channel, later confirming that it would be her sixth single released from Halcyon Days. [LINK: ([86]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-86]  On 22 January 2014, Goulding confirmed through her Facebook page that she had contributed the song " [LINK: (Beating Heart) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beating_Heart_(Ellie_Goulding_song)] " to the soundtrack for the film  [LINK: (Divergent) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Divergent_(film)] , based on the  [LINK: (novel of the same name) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Divergent_(novel)]  by  [LINK: (Veronica Roth) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Veronica_Roth] . [LINK: ([87]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-87] 
On 3 February 2014, Goulding released a cover of the James Blake song "Life Round Here" featuring rapper  [LINK: (Angel Haze) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Angel_Haze]  through her SoundCloud page. [LINK: ([88]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-88]  On 19 February, Goulding won Best British Female Solo Artist at the  [LINK: (2014 Brit Awards) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2014_Brit_Awards] . [LINK: ([89]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-89] 
On 20 October 2014, she stated via  [LINK: (Facebook) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Facebook]  that she will appear on the new  [LINK: (Calvin Harris) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calvin_Harris]  album,  [LINK: (Motion) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Motion_(Calvin_Harris_album)] , with a new song called " [LINK: (Outside) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Outside_(Calvin_Harris_song)] ". The song was released as the album's fourth single on 20 October 2014. [LINK: ([90]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-90]  Goulding also featured in  [LINK: (Iggy Azalea) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iggy_Azalea] 's song " [LINK: (Heavy Crown) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heavy_Crown_(song)] ", which was released on 21 November 2014 on Azalea's  [LINK: (Reclassified) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reclassified] , a reissue of her debut album  [LINK: (The New Classic) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_New_Classic] . [LINK: ([91]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-91]

In November 2014, Goulding announced that she was focusing on a third studio album. In early 2015, Goulding released the song " [LINK: (Love Me Like You Do) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Love_Me_Like_You_Do] ", which was featured in the soundtrack to the film  [LINK: (Fifty Shades of Grey) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fifty_Shades_of_Grey_(film)] , adapted from the  [LINK: (erotic novel of the same name) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fifty_Shades_of_Grey] . The video was released to  [LINK: (YouTube) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/YouTube]  on 22 January, to precede an official release date of 15 February. [LINK: ([92]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-92]  The single has been a commercial success, spending four weeks at No. 1 on the  [LINK: (UK Singles Chart) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/UK_Singles_Chart] , topping the charts in many other nations including Australia, New Zealand, and Germany, and reaching No. 3 on the US  [LINK: (Billboard Hot 100) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Billboard_Hot_100] . The single held the record for the most-streamed track in a single week in the United Kingdom (streamed 2.58 million times), and worldwide (streamed 15.5 million times). [LINK: ([93]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-93]  On 7 December 2015, "Love Me like You Do" earned Goulding a  [LINK: (Grammy Award) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grammy_Award]  nomination for  [LINK: (Best Pop Solo Performance) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grammy_Award_for_Best_Pop_Solo_Performance] . [LINK: ([2]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-58Grammys-2]  In the nominations for the  [LINK: (2016 Brit Awards) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2016_Brit_Awards]  announced on 14 January 2016, the song was among the nominees for British Single of the Year, and Best British Video. [LINK: ([94]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-94]  Goulding starred in the music video for  [LINK: (Taylor Swift) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taylor_Swift] 's song " [LINK: (Bad Blood) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bad_Blood_(Taylor_Swift_song)] ", which was released in May 2015. [LINK: ([95]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-95]

Goulding appeared on the  [LINK: (Major Lazer) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Major_Lazer]  album  [LINK: (Peace Is the Mission) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peace_Is_the_Mission]  on the track " [LINK: (Powerful) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Powerful_(song)] ", alongside  [LINK: (Tarrus Riley) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tarrus_Riley] . The track was released together with the album on 1 June 2015. A preview of the single was revealed on 23 April 2015. [LINK: ([96]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-96]  Having finished recording new material on 27 July 2015, Goulding tweeted a link to an Instagram post of her leaving  [LINK: (Abbey Road Studios) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abbey_Road_Studios]  captioned, "That's a wrap!". [LINK: ([97]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-97]  On 5 August 2015 at the  [LINK: (iHeartRadio) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IHeartRadio]  Music Summit, Interscope unveiled the title of Goulding's new single, " [LINK: (On My Mind) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/On_My_Mind_(Ellie_Goulding_song)] ". [LINK: ([98]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-98]  A preview of the new track was released online via Goulding's Facebook page on 15 September 2015, with a confirmed single release date of 17 September 2015. The following day, another video teaser was uploaded revealing the title and cover art for Goulding's third studio album,  [LINK: (Delirium) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Delirium_(Ellie_Goulding_album)] .

On 7 September 2015, it was announced that Goulding would be performing at the  [LINK: (2015 AFL Grand Final) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2015_AFL_Grand_Final] , along with Canadian musician  [LINK: (Bryan Adams) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bryan_Adams]  and American musician  [LINK: (Chris Isaak) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chris_Isaak] . [LINK: ([99]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-99]  On 17 September, Goulding debuted her single, "On My Mind", the lead track from Delirium, on BBC Radio 1's Breakfast Show. She also announced that Delirium would be released on 6 November. Goulding subsequently performed "On My Mind" at the  [LINK: (Apple Music Festival) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apple_Music_Festival]  later that week. [LINK: ([100]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-100]  [LINK: ([101]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-101]

Goulding also appeared on the Australian  [LINK: (X Factor) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_X_Factor_(Australian_TV_series)]  on 6 October where she performed "On My Mind". [LINK: ([102]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-102]  On 15 October 2015, it was announced that " [LINK: (Army) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Army_(Ellie_Goulding_song)] " would serve as the second official single from the album; the song's music video was later released on 14 January 2016. [LINK: ([103]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-103]  Third single, " [LINK: (Something in the Way You Move) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Something_in_the_Way_You_Move] " was first released as a promotional single from the album on 9 October 2015. [LINK: ([104]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-104]  It was then released on 19 January 2016, its original music video was released on 23 February 2016 [LINK: ([105]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-105]  and other music video directed by  [LINK: (Emil Nava) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emil_Nava]  was released on 21 June 2017. [LINK: ([106]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-106]

On 19 August 2016 she released the song " [LINK: (Still Falling for You) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Still_Falling_for_You] " for the  [LINK: (soundtrack) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bridget_Jones%27s_Baby:_Original_Motion_Picture_Soundtrack]  to the film  [LINK: (Bridget Jones's Baby) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bridget_Jones%27s_Baby] , and its music video premiered on 25 August 2016. [LINK: ([107]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-107]  [LINK: ([108]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-108]  It received moderate commercial success worldwide managing to reach number 11 in the UK. [LINK: ([29]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-UK_chart-29]  After taking some months off, in 2017, she performed at the opening of 16th edition of  [LINK: (Mawazine) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mawazine]  Festival, held in Rabat from 12 to 20 May. [LINK: ([109]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-109]  [LINK: ([110]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-110]

During that period of time, Goulding announced that she was taking some time out the spotlight due to illness, which lasted five years, meanwhile most of her releases were singles in forms of collaborations with other artists or for movie soundtracks. [LINK: ([111]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-111]  [LINK: ([112]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-herHealth-112]

Her first stand-alone release was a collaboration with  [LINK: (Kygo) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kygo] , which she previously premiered at the opening of the Mawazine Festival. The single titled, " [LINK: (First Time) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/First_Time_(Kygo_and_Ellie_Goulding_song)] ", was released on 28 April 2017. [LINK: ([113]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-113]

In 2018, Goulding joined Tap Management after almost a decade with First Access Management. [LINK: ([114]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-114]  She appeared on a collaboration with  [LINK: (Sean Paul) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sean_Paul]  on his  [LINK: (Mad Love the Prequel) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mad_Love_the_Prequel]  EP titled "Bad Love", released on 29 June 2018. [LINK: ([115]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-115]

Goulding collaborated with  [LINK: (Diplo) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diplo]  and  [LINK: (Swae Lee) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Swae_Lee]  on the single " [LINK: (Close to Me) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Close_to_Me_(Ellie_Goulding_and_Diplo_song)] ", which was released on 24 October 2018. [LINK: ([116]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-116]  On 1 January 2019, The Guardian reported that she has been working on her fourth album, set to release in the same year. [LINK: ([117]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-117]  On 1 March, she released the next single " [LINK: (Flux) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flux_(Ellie_Goulding_song)] ". [LINK: ([118]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-118]  She said regarding the album, "It's very much written by me". [LINK: ([119]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-119]

On 12 April 2019, Goulding released the single " [LINK: (Sixteen) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sixteen_(Ellie_Goulding_song)] ". [LINK: ([120]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-120]  Goulding said of the single, "...That age was such a pivotal year for me in many ways and this song is so close to my heart. It takes me back to the reckless days of being a teenager and I hope it reminds us all about the innocence of youth." [LINK: ([121]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-sixteen_billboard-121]

Goulding released " [LINK: (Hate Me) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hate_Me_(Ellie_Goulding_and_Juice_Wrld_song)] " with American rapper  [LINK: (Juice Wrld) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Juice_Wrld]  on 26 June 2019. [LINK: ([122]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-Official-122]  It was premiered by  [LINK: (Zane Lowe) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zane_Lowe]  as his 'World Record' on  [LINK: (Beats 1) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beats_1] . [LINK: ([123]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-Billboard-123]  In July, Goulding started teasing her return and stated that her next material to be released would be the songs "Woman I Am" and "Start". [LINK: ([124]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-124]  In November, she released  [LINK: (her rendition) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/River_(Joni_Mitchell_song)#Ellie_Goulding_version]  of  [LINK: (Joni Mitchell) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joni_Mitchell] 's Christmas song " [LINK: (River) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/River_(Joni_Mitchell_song)] ", which topped the UK Singles Chart, becoming her third UK number one single and the last UK number one song of the 2010s. [LINK: ([125]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-125]

On 2020, Goulding came back out of her hiatus and started teasing her next release. On 13 March 2020, Goulding released the single " [LINK: (Worry About Me) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Worry_About_Me] " which was created in-collaboration with  [LINK: (Blackbear) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blackbear_(musician)] . [LINK: ([126]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-126]  In a radio interview with  [LINK: (Heart) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heart_(radio_network)]  the same month, she revealed that the album "kind of comes in two parts", adding that "the first side is something written entirely by me which was fun and I wrote most of it in New York when I was living there a few years back. I play the guitar and I play the bass and piano and then I'm singing a lot of vocals. It's very classically influenced because I love classical music. There's a lot going on, it's a big soundscape and one big film. The second half is my kind of alter ego songs." [LINK: ([127]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-127]  On 21 May she released single " [LINK: (Power) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Power_(Ellie_Goulding_song)] " and on 30 June single " [LINK: (Slow Grenade) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slow_Grenade] " with  [LINK: (Lauv) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lauv] .

Goulding released her fourth studio album,  [LINK: (Brightest Blue) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brightest_Blue] , on 17 July 2020. Originally scheduled for 5 June 2020, the album's release was delayed due to the  [LINK: (COVID-19 pandemic) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/COVID-19_pandemic] . The album debuted at the top of the  [LINK: (UK Album Chart) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/UK_Albums_Chart] , becoming Goulding's third album to do so, [LINK: ([128]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-128]  as well as at No. 2 in  [LINK: (Scotland) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scotland] . [LINK: ([129]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-129]  It reached the top 10 in  [LINK: (Ireland) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ireland]  [LINK: ([130]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-130]  as well as the top 40 in over ten countries including  [LINK: (Australia) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australia] ,  [LINK: (Germany) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Germany]  and the  [LINK: (United States) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States] .

Goulding announced on an Instagram Q&A that she would be releasing new music which was not part of the Brightest Blue era at the end of January 2021. [LINK: ([131]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-131]  On 21 January, she released a collaboration with electronic duo  [LINK: (Silk City) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silk_City_(duo)] , titled " [LINK: (New Love) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_Love_(Silk_City_song)] ". [LINK: ([132]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-132]  On 30 September, Goulding performed " [LINK: (Anything Could Happen) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anything_Could_Happen] " as part of the opening ceremony for  [LINK: (Expo 2020) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Expo_2020] , held in  [LINK: (Dubai) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dubai] . [LINK: ([133]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-133]

On 19 June 2022, Goulding performed at  [LINK: (Rock in Rio) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rock_in_Rio#Rock_in_Rio_Lisboa_(2022)]  in  [LINK: (Lisbon) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lisbon] , Portugal. After the concert, she announced that she would be releasing new music in July. The following day, she blacked out all her social media profiles. [LINK: ([134]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-134]  Back in July 2021, during an interview with  [LINK: (Joe Wicks) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joe_Wicks_(coach)] , she described the forthcoming album as "a dance record. It's electronic pop, a dance thing from outer space". [LINK: ([135]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-135]  On 4 July 2022, she announced the release of " [LINK: (Easy Lover) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Easy_Lover_(Ellie_Goulding_song)] " featuring  [LINK: (Big Sean) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Big_Sean] , which was released on 15 July. [LINK: ([136]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-136]  The single did not enter the UK Singles Top 100, but peaked at number 31 on the UK Singles Downloads Chart Top 100. [LINK: ([137]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-137]  It was followed by " [LINK: (All by Myself) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/All_by_Myself_(Alok,_Sigala_and_Ellie_Goulding_song)] ", a collaboration between Goulding and producers  [LINK: (Alok) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alok_(DJ)]  and  [LINK: (Sigala) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sigala] , on 7 October. [LINK: ([138]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-138]  Goulding released the single " [LINK: (Let It Die) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Let_It_Die_(Ellie_Goulding_song)] " along with its video on 19 October and announced the same day that her fifth studio album,  [LINK: (Higher Than Heaven) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Higher_Than_Heaven] , would be released on 3 February 2023. [LINK: ([139]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-139]  [LINK: ([140]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-140]  It was delayed multiple times and released on 7 April 2023. [LINK: ([141]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-141]

On 10 March Goulding released her third collaboration with Harris, " [LINK: (Miracle) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Miracle_(Calvin_Harris_and_Ellie_Goulding_song)] " which was met with both commercial and critical success, it marked Goulding's comeback to the singles chart, especially in the United Kingdom, where it debuted at number three, and eventually went to top the UK Singles Chart, becoming Goulding fourth chart-topper. [LINK: ([142]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-142]  In its second week at number one, Goulding's album Higher Than Heaven also topped the UK Albums Chart, marking the first time Goulding  [LINK: (simultaneously had a number-one single and album) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_artists_who_have_achieved_simultaneous_number-one_UK_Single_and_Album]  in her career. [LINK: ([143]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-143]  The album became Goulding's fourth chart-topper effort, tying her with Adele as the British female acts with most number one albums in history. [LINK: ([144]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-144]  Meanwhile, "Miracle" stayed atop the chart for eight non-consecutive weeks, becoming Goulding's longest-running number-one to date. [LINK: ([145]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-145]  With "Miracle", Goulding earned her second  [LINK: (Grammy) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grammy_Awards]  nomination for  [LINK: (Best Pop Dance Recording) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grammy_Award_for_Best_Dance_Pop_Recording] , and a  [LINK: (Brit Award) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brit_Awards]  nomination for  [LINK: (Song of the Year) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brit_Award_for_Song_of_the_Year] . [LINK: ([146]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-146]  [LINK: ([147]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-147]  As of 26 July 2024 the single is certified two-time platinum by the  [LINK: (BPI) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/British_Phonographic_Industry] . [LINK: ([148]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-148]

On 22 March 2023, Goulding released the single " [LINK: (By the End of the Night) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/By_The_End_of_the_Night] ". [LINK: ([149]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-149]  [LINK: ([150]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-150]  On 3 May Goulding was presented by the  [LINK: (British Phonographic Industry) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/British_Phonographic_Industry]  with the prestigious  [LINK: (BRIT Billion Award) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brits_Billion_Award] . [LINK: ([151]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-151]

On 14 September, Goulding released the single " [LINK: (Somebody) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Somebody_(TSHA,_Ellie_Goulding_and_Gregory_Porter_song)] ", in collaboration with TSHA and  [LINK: (Gregory Porter) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gregory_Porter] . [LINK: ([152]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-152]  [LINK: ([153]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-153]  On 13 October, Goulding joined Japanese musician  [LINK: (Yoshiki) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yoshiki_(musician)]  on stage at Royal Albert Hall to perform a classical version of "Love Me Like You Do". [LINK: ([154]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-154]

On 18 April 2024, Goulding surprise released a remixed version of her song "Brightest Blue" in collaboration with  [LINK: (Nature) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nature] , with the purpose of using the royalties of the song to help environmental causes. [LINK: ([155]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-155]  On 28 Apri, during a one-night-only concert at the Royal Albert Hall, Goulding performed a new song titled, "Easy To Love Me", and hinted that it would be part of her upcoming sixth studio album as she stated that she was working on new music. [LINK: ([156]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-156]  On 30 April Goulding shared that she was working with producer Jack Rochon for her sixth studio album via her Instagram stories. [LINK: ([157]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-157]

After the immense success of their third collaboration, Goulding and Harris hinted the possibility of working together again. On 9 July Harris teased his new collaboration with Goulding in Ibiza. [LINK: ([158]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-158]  On 19 July the date of release, the title and artwork of the single were announced by Harris. [LINK: ([159]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-159]  On 25 July the duo performed the single for the first time live in Ibiza. [LINK: ([160]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-160]  On 26 July the music duo released their fourth collaboration " [LINK: (Free) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Free_(Calvin_Harris_and_Ellie_Goulding_song)] ". [LINK: ([161]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-161]  [LINK: ([162]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-162]  Goulding provided the lead vocals for  [LINK: (Starsmith) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Starsmith] 's comeback single, " [LINK: (Leave Me Slowly) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leave_Me_Slowly_(Starsmith_song)] ", which was released on 16 August. [LINK: ([163]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-163]  [LINK: ([164]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-164]  [LINK: ([165]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-165]

On 8 May 2024,  [LINK: (Four Tet) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Four_Tet]  teased a new single with Goulding on his social media, titled " [LINK: (In My Dreams) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/In_My_Dreams_(Four_Tet_and_Ellie_Goulding_song)] ". [LINK: ([166]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-166]  It marks their fifth collaboration and first since the  [LINK: (Grammy-nominated remix) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grammy_Award_for_Best_Remixed_Recording,_Non-Classical]  of " [LINK: (Easy Lover) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Easy_Lover_(Ellie_Goulding_song)] ". [LINK: ([167]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-167]  The single was released on 9 September 2024. [LINK: ([168]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-168]  [LINK: ([169]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-169]  On 7 October DJ  [LINK: (Hugel) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hugel_(DJ)]  teased an upcoming remix of his hit single " [LINK: (I Adore You) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/I_Adore_You_(Hugel,_Topic_and_Arash_song)] " with Goulding and  [LINK: (J Balvin) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/J_Balvin] . [LINK: ([170]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-170]  Goulding and Balvin's remix of the song was officially released on 15 November. [LINK: ([171]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-171]  On 2 December, during a press conference, before her performance at the sold-out Top of the Mountain opening concert in  [LINK: (Ischgl) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ischgl] , Austria, Goulding was interviewed by  [LINK: (The Sun) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Sun_(United_Kingdom)] , and she revealed that her sixth studio album would be "very personal", and stated that she has a classical album set to be released. [LINK: ([172]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-172]  [LINK: ([173]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-173]  On 29 December Goulding joined DJ and producer  [LINK: (Anyma) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anyma]  as a surprise guest to perform on his  [LINK: (Sphere) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sphere_(venue)]  residency in  [LINK: (Las Vegas) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Las_Vegas]  to debut an unreleased song, titled " [LINK: (Hypnotized) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hypnotized_(Anyma_and_Ellie_Goulding_song)] ". [LINK: ([174]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-174]  [LINK: ([175]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-175]  The song was released on 10 January 2025 to widespread critical acclaim, with Goulding's vocal performance achieving unanimous praise by  [LINK: (music critics) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_journalism] . [LINK: ([176]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-176]  [LINK: ([177]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-177]

On 29 April it was announced that Goulding would serve as the narrator, and music composer, alongside Jim Fairfield, of environmental documentary Bee Wild, directed by Rebecca and  [LINK: (Josh Tickell) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Josh_Tickell] . [LINK: ([178]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-Balaga-178]  The documentary premiered on 5 June at the  [LINK: (SXSW London) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_by_Southwest]  film festival. [LINK: ([178]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-Balaga-178]  [LINK: ([179]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-imdb.com-179]  On 6 June Goulding collaborated with DJs  [LINK: (Marshmello) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marshmello]  and AVAION on the  [LINK: (House) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/House_music]  single " [LINK: (Save My Love) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Save_My_Love_(Marshmello,_Ellie_Goulding_and_AVAION_song)] " which was met with favourable reviews. [LINK: ([180]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-180]  [LINK: ([181]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-Volpe-181]  On 10 June it was announced that Goulding will contribute with the closing theme song for the  [LINK: (dark fantasy) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dark_fantasy]   [LINK: (anime) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anime]  series  [LINK: (Clevatess) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clevatess] , with the original song " [LINK: (Destiny) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Destiny_(Ellie_Goulding_song)] ". [LINK: ([182]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-182]  [LINK: ([183]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-183]  The track was later released as a single on 12 November. [LINK: ([184]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-184]

In June 2025 Goulding attended the  [LINK: (wedding of Jeff Bezos and Lauren Sánchez) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wedding_of_Jeff_Bezos_and_Lauren_S%C3%A1nchez]  in  [LINK: (Venice) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Venice] , Italy, and performed her cover of "Your Song". [LINK: ([185]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-185]  [LINK: ([186]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-186]


# ARTISTRY #

Goulding has listed  [LINK: (Joni Mitchell) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joni_Mitchell] ,  [LINK: (Kate Bush) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kate_Bush] , and  [LINK: (Björk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bj%C3%B6rk]  as influences, as well as contemporaries such as  [LINK: (Amy Winehouse) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amy_Winehouse] ,  [LINK: (Katy Perry) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Katy_Perry] ,  [LINK: (Lady Gaga) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lady_Gaga] ,  [LINK: (Beyoncé) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beyonc%C3%A9] ,  [LINK: (Burial) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burial_(musician)] ,  [LINK: (Taylor Swift) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taylor_Swift] ,  [LINK: (Bon Iver) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bon_Iver] , and  [LINK: (Rihanna) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rihanna] . [LINK: ([187]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-187]  [LINK: ([188]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-188]  [LINK: ([189]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-189]  [LINK: ([190]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-190]  [LINK: ([191]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-191]  [LINK: ([192]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-192]  She also expressed admiration for rappers  [LINK: (Kanye West) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kanye_West] ,  [LINK: (Drake) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Drake_(rapper)]  and  [LINK: (Nicki Minaj) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nicki_Minaj] . [LINK: ([193]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-193]

Goulding's music has been described as  [LINK: (electropop) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electropop] , [LINK: ([194]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-194]  [LINK: ([195]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-195]   [LINK: (synthpop) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Synthpop] , [LINK: ([196]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-196]   [LINK: (indie pop) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indie_pop]  [LINK: ([197]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-197]  and  [LINK: (folktronica) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Folktronica] . [LINK: ([198]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-198]  [LINK: ([199]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-199]  Her musical style has been compared to the likes of  [LINK: (Kate Nash) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kate_Nash] ,  [LINK: (Lykke Li) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lykke_Li]  and  [LINK: (Tracey Thorn) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tracey_Thorn] . [LINK: ([200]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-200]

Goulding's debut album  [LINK: (Lights) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lights_(Ellie_Goulding_album)]  (2010) experimented with genres including indie pop, synthpop, folktronica and indietronica. The album contained "sparkling pop with a  [LINK: (folky) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Folk_music]  heart and an  [LINK: (electronic) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electronic_music]  edge" and was noted as being infectious. [LINK: ([201]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-thefly-201]  The album incorporated "acoustic guitar" and "retro-synthpop" compared to that of  [LINK: (Little Boots) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Little_Boots]  and  [LINK: (La Roux) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/La_Roux] , while the production contained "folkie origins under a welter of busily cycling synths and programmed beats". [LINK: ([202]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-independent-202]  Goulding's second album  [LINK: (Halcyon) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Halcyon_(album)]  (2012) followed in the same vein, including genres such as indie pop, synthpop and  [LINK: (dream pop) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dream_pop] . She stepped away from the electronic sound of her previous album and moved to a more tribal and anthemic sound containing a bit more piano and vocal. [LINK: ([203]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-203]  Its re-issue  [LINK: (Halcyon Days) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Halcyon_Days_(Ellie_Goulding_album)]  (2013), which features ten new songs, marked Goulding's return to electropop. She spoke in an interview with  [LINK: (Elle) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elle_(magazine)]  about the reason behind her return to a more electronic sound, stating: "I have such an affinity with electronic music that I can't step away from it." [LINK: ([204]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-204]

Goulding's third studio album  [LINK: (Delirium) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Delirium_(Ellie_Goulding_album)]  (2015) marked a shift to a more maximalist sound. [LINK: ([205]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-205]  Rooted in  [LINK: (pop music) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pop_music] , it incorporated genres such as electropop, synthpop,  [LINK: (dance) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dance_music] ,  [LINK: (R&B) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/R%26B] , and  [LINK: (folk-pop) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Folk-pop] . [LINK: ([206]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-206]  Delirium divided  [LINK: (music critics) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_journalism]  and fans alike, with critics praising its production but finding that its lyrics lacked personality in comparison to her previous albums. [LINK: ([207]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-207]  [LINK: ([208]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-208]  Goulding's fourth studio album  [LINK: (Brightest Blue) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brightest_Blue]  (2020) is divided in two sides. The first side, which was described as recapturing the "simplicity" and "vulnerability" of her first two records, experiments with genres such as R&B,  [LINK: (soul) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soul_music]  and electropop. [LINK: ([209]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-209]  Meanwhile, the second side EG.0 incorporates influences from music genres like  [LINK: (hip-hop) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hip-hop]  and dance. [LINK: ([210]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-210]  Goulding's fifth studio album  [LINK: (Higher Than Heaven) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Higher_Than_Heaven]  (2023) is primarily a  [LINK: (dance-pop) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dance-pop]  and  [LINK: (nu-disco) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nu-disco]  record with elements of synthpop, R&B and EDM. [LINK: ([211]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-211]  [LINK: ([212]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-212]

Goulding is a  [LINK: (soprano) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soprano]  [LINK: ([213]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-213]  [LINK: ([214]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-214]  [LINK: ([215]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-Paste-215]  and is noted for her high piercing  [LINK: (vibrato) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vibrato] , breathy tone and emotive delivery. [LINK: ([216]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-216]  [LINK: ([217]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-217]  [LINK: ([218]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-usatoday-218]

In a review for Halcyon,  [LINK: (Neil McCormick) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neil_McCormick]  of  [LINK: (The Daily Telegraph) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Daily_Telegraph]  described her voice as "something special", continuing; "Her tremulous vibrato and slightly hoarse  [LINK: (timbre) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timbre]  have the feel of something primal and folky, her birdlike high notes conveying a childlike wonder while darker tones imply ancient depths of sorrow. She sings like she is strung out on the melody, warbling from a place of desperate emotion. It really is that rarest and perhaps most accidental of gifts: an original voice". He then continued in regards to her vocal layering stating, "producer Jim Eliot puts her voice front, back and centre, banking up choral walls of vibrato, fashioning hooks from cut up samples of chirrups and chants, and creating unusual textures from trills and warbles". [LINK: ([219]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-219]  During an interview with  [LINK: (Carson Daly) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carson_Daly] , Goulding described her own voice saying;

I think sometimes it sounds like my voice is like, out of control... I have to really control it because it just kind of goes everywhere. Like, sometimes stuff comes out that I don't expect. A lot, actually [...]. It's so funny because my favourite thing to do is imitate opera singers, but I've never had a singing lesson. Oh, I had a lesson just to teach me how to breathe better, but I never really had a singing lesson. [LINK: ([220]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-220]

[LINK: (Will Hermes) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Will_Hermes]  of  [LINK: (Rolling Stone) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rolling_Stone]  compared her voice to that of  [LINK: (Dolly Parton) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dolly_Parton] , stating that her upper register was dazzling whilst also complementing her skill in vocal multi-layering. [LINK: ([221]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-221]  Megan Farokhmanesh of  [LINK: (Paste) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paste_(magazine)]  magazine stated "Goulding has a lovely voice, but occasionally her soprano-strung vocals hit a note that rubs the eardrums the wrong way" although she praised Goulding overall for her "talent for gorgeous high heart-tugging vocals". [LINK: ([215]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-Paste-215]

During the 2020s, critics became more appreciative of Goulding's voice, with many noticing its enduring quality and describing her vocals as ethereal. [LINK: ([222]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-222]  [LINK: ([223]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-223]  [LINK: ([181]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-Volpe-181]  In her review of Higher Than Heaven, Katie Bain from Billboard called her "one of  [LINK: (dance music) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dance_music] 's most important and enduring voices". [LINK: ([224]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-224]  Similarly, In their review of "In My Dreams", Oculate UK praised Goulding's voice as it "remains one of pop's most recognisable", while Jordi Bardají of  [LINK: (Jenesaispop) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jenesaispop]  in his review of "Hypnotized", said that Goulding's ethereal voice fits in  [LINK: (EDM) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electronic_dance_music]  productions like a glove. [LINK: ([225]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-225]  [LINK: ([226]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-226]

Goulding has received praise and admiration from fellow peers. Some artists that have spoken highly about the singer include  [LINK: (Halsey) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Halsey_(singer)] , [LINK: ([227]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-227]   [LINK: (Bridgit Mendler) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bridgit_Mendler] , [LINK: ([228]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-228]   [LINK: (Lauv) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lauv] , [LINK: ([229]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-229]   [LINK: (Camila Cabello) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Camila_Cabello] , [LINK: ([230]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-230]   [LINK: (Normani) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Normani] , [LINK: ([231]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-231]   [LINK: (Lil Nas X) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lil_Nas_X] , [LINK: ([232]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-232]   [LINK: (Alex James) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alex_James_(musician)]  of  [LINK: (Blur) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blur_(band)] , [LINK: ([233]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-Cooper-233]   [LINK: (Chappell Roan) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chappell_Roan] , [LINK: ([234]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-popcrave.com-234]   [LINK: (Ally Brooke) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ally_Brooke] , [LINK: ([235]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-235]   [LINK: (Bunt) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bunt_(DJ)] , [LINK: ([236]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-236]  Taylor Swift, [LINK: ([237]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-:3-237]   [LINK: (Aaron Paul) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aaron_Paul] , [LINK: ([238]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-238]   [LINK: (Greyson Chance) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greyson_Chance] , [LINK: ([239]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-239]   [LINK: (Sadie Jean) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sadie_Jean] , [LINK: ([240]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-240]   [LINK: (DJ Fresh) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DJ_Fresh] , [LINK: ([241]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-241]   [LINK: (Olivia Lunny) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Olivia_Lunny] , [LINK: ([242]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-242]   [LINK: (Rhea Raj) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rhea_Raj] , [LINK: ([243]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-243]   [LINK: (Calvin Harris) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calvin_Harris] , [LINK: ([244]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-244]   [LINK: (Selena Gomez) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Selena_Gomez] , [LINK: ([245]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-:4-245]  and  [LINK: (Lorde) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lorde] . [LINK: ([246]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-246]

James praised Goulding's authenticity: "Love her songs. She's the real deal in a world of bogus pop pretenders." [LINK: ([247]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-247]  [LINK: ([233]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-Cooper-233]  He also included  [LINK: (Halcyon Days) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Halcyon_Days_(Ellie_Goulding_album)]  in Blur's favourites albums of all-time on  [LINK: (iTunes) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ITunes] . [LINK: ([248]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-248]  [LINK: ([249]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-249]  Harris, a frequent collaborator of Goulding, spoke in an interview with  [LINK: (Dork) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dork_(magazine)]  about working with Goulding: "Ellie has the three good things about working with somebody. A spectacular unique voice and delivery that can carry a song emotionally, and [she's] a laugh!". [LINK: ([250]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-250]  Lorde stated in an interview with  [LINK: (Clash Magazine) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clash_(magazine)]  that she would "love to write for – or with – Ellie Goulding, actually." [LINK: ([251]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-251]  Swift praised Goulding's voice while talking with  [LINK: (Capital FM) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Capital_FM_(radio_network)] , saying: "Ellie is amazing, and when she starts singing – I remember the affect she had on my band – they were all looking at each other like 'That's really what her voice sounds like'," she explained. "Because when you first hear an Ellie Goulding song, you're like 'Oh I wonder what effect they're using on her voice. No, that's just the way it sounds." [LINK: ([237]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-:3-237]  Roan mentioned Goulding in an interview with  [LINK: (Pop Crave) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pop_Crave]  as one of the inspirations that influenced her early music. [LINK: ([234]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-popcrave.com-234]  [LINK: ([252]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-252]  Gomez cited Goulding as an influence for the making of her album  [LINK: (Stars Dance) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stars_Dance]  in an interview with  [LINK: (Teen Vogue) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Teen_Vogue] , saying: "I got to record 20 or so great songs and work with a bunch of different producers and they're all really fun, pop songs and a little Ellie Goulding-ish." [LINK: ([245]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-:4-245]


# PERSONAL LIFE #

She dated English radio DJ  [LINK: (Greg James) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greg_James]  in 2010. Their relationship ended in 2012 after 18 months together. [LINK: ([253]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-253]  In the same year, after collaborating on a song called "Bittersweet" for the Twilight: Breaking Dawn Part Two soundtrack, Goulding started dating DJ  [LINK: (Skrillex) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skrillex] . The two split nine months later, citing the long-distance nature of their relationship. [LINK: ([254]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-254]  Goulding later was in a relationship with actor  [LINK: (Jeremy Irvine) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jeremy_Irvine] . They broke up in August 2013. [LINK: ([255]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-255]  Goulding was in a relationship with  [LINK: (Dougie Poynter) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dougie_Poynter]  of  [LINK: (McFly) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/McFly]  between 2014 and 2016. [LINK: ([256]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-256]

On 7 August 2018, Goulding and her boyfriend Caspar Jopling announced their engagement. [LINK: ([257]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-257]  [LINK: ([258]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-258]  The couple were married at  [LINK: (York Minster) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/York_Minster]  on 31 August 2019, [LINK: ([259]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-259]  [LINK: ([260]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-260]  and Goulding was  [LINK: (baptised) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baptism]  in the  [LINK: (Church of England) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Church_of_England]  in order to get married. [LINK: ([261]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-261]  Jopling is the grandson of former  [LINK: (Conservative) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Conservative_Party_(UK)]  MP  [LINK: (Michael Jopling, Baron Jopling) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_Jopling] . [LINK: ([262]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-262]  In February 2021, Goulding announced that she and Jopling were expecting their first child. [LINK: ([263]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-263]  She gave birth to a son in April 2021. [LINK: ([264]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-264]  [LINK: ([265]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-265]  In February 2024, Goulding and Jopling announced their separation. [LINK: ([266]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-266]  [LINK: ([267]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-267]  Following the separation, she began dating American actor Beau Minniear, who appeared in the music video for her single " [LINK: (Destiny) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Destiny_(Ellie_Goulding_song)] " (2025). [LINK: ([268]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-268]  In December 2025, she revealed that she was expecting her second child and first with Minniear. [LINK: ([269]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-269]  [LINK: ([270]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-270]

Goulding's best friend and personal assistant is Hannah Suzanne Lowe; the 2015 song " [LINK: (Army) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Army_(Ellie_Goulding_song)] " was dedicated to Lowe and to Goulding's fans. [LINK: ([271]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-271]  [LINK: ([272]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-272]  On  [LINK: (Michael McIntyre's Big Show) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_McIntyre%27s_Big_Show] , she revealed that she is also close friends with  [LINK: (Princess Beatrice of York) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Princess_Beatrice_of_York] . [LINK: ([273]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-273]

Goulding ran the inaugural Nike Women Half Marathon in Washington, D.C. on 28 April 2013, earning a time of 1:41:35. [LINK: ([274]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-274]  [LINK: ([275]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-275]

Goulding has spoken several times about her ongoing experiences with  [LINK: (mental health) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mental_health]  conditions, which includes struggles with a chronic  [LINK: (anxiety disorder) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anxiety_disorder] ,  [LINK: (panic attacks) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Panic_attack] ,  [LINK: (imposter syndrome) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Impostor_syndrome] , and post-natal depression. [LINK: ([276]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-stylist.co.uk-276]  [LINK: ([277]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-277]  [LINK: ([278]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-278]

"I get such chronic  [LINK: (anxiety) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anxiety]  that in the rare moments I don't have anxiety, I feel so happy and full of joy that I'm not having it. If I am in an anxious state, I don't feel things. I numb myself to everything."

In 2016, she spoke to  [LINK: (Flare) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flare_(magazine)]  about suffering panic attacks caused by the studio environment that prevented her from working, and going to  [LINK: (cognitive behavioural therapy) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cognitive_behavioral_therapy]  sessions for the first time. [LINK: ([280]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-280]  In 2017, she discussed in an interview with  [LINK: (Well+Good) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Well%2BGood] , her ongoing confidence issues and severe  [LINK: (anxiety) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Generalized_anxiety_disorder]  she had experienced. [LINK: ([112]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-herHealth-112]  In 2019, a week after the  [LINK: (World Mental Health Day) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_Mental_Health_Day] , Goulding used her  [LINK: (Instagram) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Instagram]  account to bring awareness on dealing with imposter syndrome, sharing her own experience with it and the consequences it had in her life and career. [LINK: ([276]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-stylist.co.uk-276]  She also revealed that her grandfather committed  [LINK: (suicide) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Suicide]  "a few years ago". [LINK: ([276]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-stylist.co.uk-276]  [LINK: ([281]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-281]  In December 2023, whilst guest editing  [LINK: (the Today) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Today_(BBC_Radio_4)]  programme, she revealed that she had suffered from  [LINK: (post-natal depression) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Post-natal_depression]  following the birth of her son in 2021. [LINK: ([282]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-282]  Goulding credits her approach to the natural environment, having a fitness regime, and  [LINK: (kickboxing) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kickboxing]  as ways that helped her overcome panic attacks and anxiety. [LINK: ([283]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-283]  [LINK: ([284]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-284]  [LINK: ([285]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-285]

Goulding formerly followed a  [LINK: (plant-based diet) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plant-based_diet] . [LINK: ([286]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-286]


# PUBLIC IMAGE #

Goulding's personal life has been highly subject of intense media scrutiny, [LINK: ([287]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-287]  [LINK: ([288]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-:9-288]  [LINK: ([289]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-289]  as well a victim of constant false rumours spread by  [LINK: (British tabloids) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tabloid_journalism] , which has affected her public image and her mental health. [LINK: ([290]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-290]  [LINK: ([291]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-291]  [LINK: ([292]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-292]  [LINK: ([293]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-293]  [LINK: ([294]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-294]  Goulding stated that the media coverage of her life felt like "being strapped to a space shuttle". [LINK: ([295]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-295]

After the release of the song " [LINK: (Don't) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Don%27t_(Ed_Sheeran_song)] " by  [LINK: (Ed Sheeran) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ed_Sheeran] , Goulding was rumoured to be the subject person behind the lyrical content, which Goulding denied multiple times, clarifying that she has never dated Sheeran. [LINK: ([296]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-296]  [LINK: ([297]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-297]  The media coverage and subsequent  [LINK: (slut-shame) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slut-shame]  received over the false claims, [LINK: ([288]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-:9-288]  led Goulding to step out from the spotlight on a five-year gap. [LINK: ([298]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-298]  [LINK: ([299]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-299]  She has expressed her disappointment and frustration with the unfounded allegations, stating: "I was made to feel like a terrible person and I really struggled with that because I know I'm not." [LINK: ([300]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-300]  [LINK: ([301]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-301]

In 2024, Goulding released a statement on her  [LINK: (Instagram stories) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Instagram_Stories]  condemning the false narratives surrounding the end of her marriage, criticising the tabloids for violating her privacy which has damaged her mental health, [LINK: ([302]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-:1-302]  she denounced the several unethical practices that the  [LINK: (media) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mass_media_in_the_United_Kingdom]  has played to get unwarranted information on her, including paying locals from  [LINK: (Costa Rica) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Costa_Rica]  to snitch information on her. [LINK: ([303]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-303]  Goulding also opened up about becoming a " [LINK: (paranoid wreck) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paranoia] " after being constantly stalked "over, and over" by an older man, as well having to deal with a male  [LINK: (paparazzi) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paparazzi]  with "a long  [LINK: (lens camera) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Camera_lens]  wrapped on a towel". [LINK: ([302]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-:1-302]  She concluded her statement saying that she "never asked for this level of intrusion". [LINK: ([302]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-:1-302]  Goulding confirmed on her  [LINK: (X) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Twitter]  account that she knows the identity of her stalker. [LINK: ([304]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-304]

During the 2020s, Goulding became a victim of  [LINK: (trolling) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trolling]  on the internet, mainly after a  [LINK: (parody account) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parody] , Fake Showbiz News, used the singer as a vessel for fake quotes on  [LINK: (X) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Twitter] , [LINK: ([305]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-305]  which quickly become a  [LINK: (viral) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meme]  trend on the internet with several users creating their own fake quotes of Goulding. [LINK: ([306]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-306]  [LINK: ([307]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-307]  Goulding has acknowledged the trend and played along with it. [LINK: ([308]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-308]  [LINK: ([309]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-309]


# PHILANTHROPY #

Goulding has dedicated herself to using her platform to advocate for a range of social issues, including  [LINK: (environmental protection) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Environmental_protection] , [LINK: ([310]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-:6-310]   [LINK: (gender equality) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gender_equality] , [LINK: ([311]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-311]   [LINK: (mental health) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mental_health]  awareness, [LINK: ([312]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-312]  support for the  [LINK: (homeless) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Homelessness_in_England] , [LINK: ([313]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-:8-313]  the victims of  [LINK: (sexual harassment) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sexual_harassment]  in the music industry, [LINK: ([314]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-314]  and  [LINK: (LGBTQ+) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/LGBTQ_people]  rights. [LINK: ([315]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-:7-315]

In 2010, Goulding participated in the  [LINK: (Bupa Great North Run) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_North_Run]  for the  [LINK: (British Heart Foundation) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/British_Heart_Foundation] . [LINK: ([316]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-316]  In 2011, Goulding ran the She Runs LA event for charity  [LINK: (Students Run LA) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Students_Run_LA] , which aims to increase access to sport for less privileged children across the  [LINK: (Los Angeles Unified School District) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Los_Angeles_Unified_School_District] . [LINK: ([317]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-317]

In 2012, she partnered with  [LINK: (Pandora Radio) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pandora_Radio] , one dollar for each sale of her mixtape was donated to the Free the Children charity. [LINK: ([318]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-318]  [LINK: ([319]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-319]  On 1 June 2013, Goulding performed at  [LINK: (Gucci) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gucci] 's global concert event in London whose campaign "Chime for Change" aims to raise awareness of women's issues in terms of education, health and justice. [LINK: ([320]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-320]

Goulding is also a supporter for helping the  [LINK: (homeless) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Homelessness] . Goulding has frequently contributed to the  [LINK: (BBC) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BBC] 's annual charity telethon  [LINK: (Children in Need) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Children_in_Need]  in the UK. [LINK: ([321]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-BBC_2016-321]  In 2013, Goulding's track "How Long Will I Love You" was the official single for the  [LINK: (2013 Children in Need) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Children_in_Need_2013]  campaign. [LINK: ([321]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-BBC_2016-321]  She has performed in the annual charity concerts for the "Streets of London" charity event at the  [LINK: (Royal Albert Hall) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Royal_Albert_Hall]  from years 2014 to 2018 consecutively. [LINK: ([322]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-322]  [LINK: ([323]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-323]  On 24 December 2015, Goulding volunteered in central London at the Marylebone Project to help end homelessness and to assist in the elimination of the stereotype associated with the homeless population. She said, "It's that stigma of what a homeless person is — they abuse drugs or abuse alcohol. It's just not true, some people come from very normal backgrounds, very normal situations and something goes wrong. It can happen to all of us." [LINK: ([324]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-324]  As a patron of the Marylebone Project, Goulding attended the opening of a 24-hour drop-in centre for homeless women in London in November 2021. [LINK: ([313]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-:8-313]

On 15 November 2014, Goulding joined the charity group  [LINK: (Band Aid 30) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Band_Aid_30]  along with other British and Irish pop acts, recording a new version of the track " [LINK: (Do They Know It's Christmas?) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Do_They_Know_It%27s_Christmas%3F] " at  [LINK: (Sarm West Studios) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sarm_West_Studios]  in  [LINK: (Notting Hill) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Notting_Hill] , London, to raise money for the  [LINK: (2014 Ebola crisis) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2014_Ebola_outbreaks]  in  [LINK: (West Africa) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/West_Africa] . [LINK: ([325]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-325]

In 2016, Goulding used her platform to champion environmental causes, which includes working with organisations like the  [LINK: (World Wildlife Fund) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_Wide_Fund_for_Nature] . [LINK: ([326]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-326]  [LINK: ([327]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-independent.ie-327]  During the 2016  [LINK: (Earth Hour) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Earth_Hour]  event, Goulding urged people to share the hashtag #MakeClimateMatter on social medias, with the purpose of show governments, that the public's support for strong climate action. [LINK: ([327]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-independent.ie-327]

In 2018, Goulding joined the  [LINK: (United Nations Foundation) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_Nations_Foundation]  as a Global Ambassador. [LINK: ([328]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-:5-328]  In April 2019, Goulding and American musician  [LINK: (Steven Price) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steven_Price_(composer)]  created an original song titled "In This Together" for  [LINK: (David Attenborough) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/David_Attenborough] 's environmental documentary series Our Planet. [LINK: ([329]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-329]  In October 2019, Goulding was one of the 2,000 activists from 190 countries who spoke at the One Young World global forum, which addressed urgent global issues such as climate change, among others. [LINK: ([330]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-330]  In 2022, Goulding called out then-Prime Minister  [LINK: (Liz Truss) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liz_Truss]  on  [LINK: (Twitter) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Twitter] , urging her to take a serious stance on the climate crisis. [LINK: ([331]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-331]  In 2023, Goulding decided that her next album would feature  [LINK: (eco-friendly) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Environmentally_friendly]  packaging. Her fifth studio album, Higher Than Heaven, saw multiple delays due to difficulties sourcing sustainable materials for the album's physical formats., but eventually was released. [LINK: ([332]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-332]

After seven years, Goulding stepped down from her role as a Global Goodwill Ambassador for the  [LINK: (United Nations Environment Programme) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_Nations_Environment_Programme]  in 2024. [LINK: ([333]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-333]

"I believe it's the minimum of human decency to allow people to be their true selves to love who they love and to do whatever the fuck they want without harm, without danger, and without oppression." [...] "Now more than ever, us allies need to step up – and we will, I promise – up to the plate and shout louder than ever before to protect – and I promise we will – to protect, support, and show the ultimate love to our fellow human beings, and I promise I will do that."

Goulding has a strong following within the  [LINK: (LGBTQ+) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/LGBTQ_people]  community, and has consistently demonstrated allyship through public advocacy for their rights. [LINK: ([335]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-335]  [LINK: ([336]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-336]  [LINK: ([337]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-337]  [LINK: ([338]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-338]

In 2014, Goulding was invited to perform at the opening ceremony of the  [LINK: (Sochi Winter Olympics) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2014_Winter_Olympics]  but declined, following singer  [LINK: (Cher) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cher] 's decision to boycott the event in protest of  [LINK: (Vladimir Putin) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vladimir_Putin] 's anti-LGBTQ+ legislation in  [LINK: (Russia) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russia] , stating: "I immediately said no." about the offer. [LINK: ([339]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-339]  [LINK: ([340]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-340]  [LINK: ([341]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-341]  [LINK: ([342]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-342]  In June 2016, during her  [LINK: (Delirium World Tour) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Delirium_World_Tour]  performance in  [LINK: (North Carolina) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North_Carolina] , Goulding displayed a  [LINK: (pride flag) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pride_flag]  as a form of protest against the state's ' [LINK: (bathroom bill) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bathroom_bill] ' (HB2), which restricted the rights of LGBTQ+ individuals. [LINK: ([315]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-:7-315]

In November 2019, Goulding was set to perform at the  [LINK: (Dallas Cowboys) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dallas_Cowboys] ' halftime show, launching the  [LINK: (Salvation Army) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Salvation_Army] 's annual  [LINK: (Red Kettle) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christmas_Kettle]  campaign. [LINK: ([343]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-343]  After sharing photos of herself volunteering, fans raised concerns about the organisation's history of  [LINK: (anti-LGBTQ+) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Outline_of_LGBTQ_topics]  policies. [LINK: ([344]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-344]  In response, Goulding threatened to withdraw unless the Salvation Army made a clear commitment or donation to the LGBTQ+ community, saying: "Upon researching this, I have reached out to The Salvation Army and said that  I would have no choice but to pull out unless they very quickly make a solid, committed pledge or donation to the LGBTQ community." [LINK: ([345]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-345]  [LINK: ([346]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-346]  The Salvation Army responded reaffirming their commitment to serving all individuals regardless of sexual orientation or gender identity and clarifying that their services are provided based solely on need. [LINK: ([347]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-347]  Following this exchange, Goulding agreed to proceed with the performance. [LINK: ([348]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-348]  The backlash renewed attention to longstanding criticism of the Salvation Army's stance on LGBTQ+ inclusivity. [LINK: ([349]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-349]

In 2022, at the  [LINK: (Virgin Atlantic Attitude Awards) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Attitude_(magazine)] , Goulding urged fellow  [LINK: (allies) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Straight_ally]  to 'step up' and use their platforms to support, and protect the  [LINK: (LGBTQ) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/LGBTQ_people]  community, placing particular emphasis on  [LINK: (transgender) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Transgender]  individuals in light of the "exhausting" rising number of targeted attacks and growing hostility toward the trans community. [LINK: ([350]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-350]  [LINK: ([351]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-351]

In May 2025, Goulding was among the musicians who signed an open letter pledging "solidarity with the  [LINK: (trans) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Transgender] ,  [LINK: (non-binary) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Non-binary_gender]  and  [LINK: (intersex) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Intersex]  communities" and condemning the April 2025  [LINK: (Supreme Court ruling) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Supreme_Court_of_the_United_Kingdom]  on the definition of woman in the  [LINK: (Equality Act) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Equality_Act_2010]  and subsequent  [LINK: (EHRC) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Equality_and_Human_Rights_Commission]  guidance. [LINK: ([352]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-352]  [LINK: ([353]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-353]


# OTHER VENTURES #

Goulding acquired a significant stake in premium British  [LINK: (hard seltzer) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hard_seltzer]  brand SERVED for an undisclosed sum in June 2021. [LINK: ([354]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-354]  Goulding said she was attracted to the brand due to it being based in her childhood home of Herefordshire, as well as for the brand's eco-friendly ethos. [LINK: ([355]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-355]

In July 2022, the  [LINK: (Advertising Standards Authority (ASA)) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Advertising_Standards_Authority_(United_Kingdom)]  banned a series of Facebook posts from Goulding promoting SERVED hard seltzer. Goulding's posts claimed the drink was low in calories and contained no sugar, which the ASA ruled were not permitted nutrition claims for alcohol products. [LINK: ([356]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-356]

In January 2023, SERVED announced that it had entered into a partnership with  [LINK: (Morrisons) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Morrisons]  part of the supermarket's 'Growing British Brands' accelerator programme, which aimed at promoting "innovative and sustainable British producers". SERVED products are now available for sale 498 Morrisons stores, as well as listings in other parts of the business including Morrisons.com, and wholesale channels like Amazon. [LINK: ([357]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-357]  Later that year, SERVED also launched a series of  [LINK: (Ready To Drink cocktails) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ready_to_drink#RTD_cocktails] , including  [LINK: (Mojito) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mojito] ,  [LINK: (Passion Fruit Martini) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Porn_star_martini] , and  [LINK: (Piña Colada) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pi%C3%B1a_colada]  flavours. [LINK: ([358]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-358]

In September 2023, Goulding announced that  [LINK: (Heineken UK) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heineken_N.V.]  had acquired a significant minority stake in SERVED. [LINK: ([359]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-359]  [LINK: ([360]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-360]

In July 2024, It was reported that SERVED was being promoted with its biggest campaign yet, the new four-week campaign consisted on several adverts under the slogan "Summer's Too Short for Bad Cocktails", those adverts were expected to be seen by over 4.5 million adults and 46% of Londoners, achieving 160 million impressions. [LINK: ([361]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-361]  The campaign will also focus on advertising throughout social media, including Goulding's own social platforms which have a combined of 30m followers. [LINK: ([362]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-362]

In 2015, Goulding and  [LINK: (MAC cosmetics) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MAC_Cosmetics]  announced their first collaboration, [LINK: ([363]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-363]  launching a set of  [LINK: (make-up) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cosmetics]  which are described on MAC's press release as an inspiration of Goulding's "light and dichotomy so present in her artwork and as a performer". [LINK: ([364]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-364]  The set of products were made available in January 2016, and each cosmetics was named after a song from Goulding's discography. [LINK: ([365]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-365]  As of May 2017, Goulding's collection is included among the best-selling MAC collaborations of all time, placing at number sixteen. [LINK: ([366]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-366]

In 2025, Goulding partnered with wellness executive Gemma Feare, and nutrition entrepreneur Jonathan Relph, launching Everystate (stylised as every•state), [LINK: ([367]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-367]  a wellness company which develops  [LINK: (mushroom supplements) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edible_mushroom] . [LINK: ([368]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-368]  [LINK: ([369]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-369]  According the press release the supplements will help to relax, have mental health clarity, and better skin. [LINK: ([370]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-370]  [LINK: ([371]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-371]

Goulding contributed her vocals to an advert for the British department store chain  [LINK: (John Lewis) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Lewis_(department_store)]  in 2010. [LINK: ([372]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-372]  The  [LINK: (John Lewis Christmas advert) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Lewis_Christmas_advert]  has become an annual tradition in  [LINK: (British culture) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Culture_of_the_United_Kingdom]  and one of the signals that the countdown to Christmas has begun in the UK, with Goulding performing "Your Song" for the store's 2010 campaign. [LINK: ([373]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-373]  [LINK: ([374]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-374]

In 2013, Goulding was announced as one of several new models for  [LINK: (Marks & Spencer) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marks_%26_Spencer] 's 'Womanism' campaign. Subtitled "Britain's leading ladies", the campaign saw Goulding appear alongside British women from various fields, including the actress  [LINK: (Helen Mirren) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Helen_Mirren] , double Olympic gold medal-winning boxer  [LINK: (Nicola Adams) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nicola_Adams] , and writer  [LINK: (Monica Ali) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monica_Ali] . [LINK: ([375]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-375]

Goulding is endorsing the Swiss shampoo  [LINK: (Pantene) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pantene]  Pro-V on television and on the official Pantene website under the tagline "Strong Is Beautiful". [LINK: ([376]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-376]  This campaign has been running since 21 March 2016. [LINK: ([377]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-377]

Goulding starred and performed " [LINK: (What the World Needs Now) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/What_the_World_Needs_Now_Is_Love] " on a new advert for  [LINK: (People's Postcode Lottery) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/People%27s_Postcode_Lottery]  2024 campaign, which thanks its players for helping to raise money for many charities in the UK. [LINK: ([378]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-378]  [LINK: ([379]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-379]


# ACCOLADES AND ACHIEVEMENTS #

Goulding has won several awards during her music career, such as two  [LINK: (Brit Awards) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brit_Awards] , a  [LINK: (Brit Billion Award) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brits_Billion_Award] , a  [LINK: (Billboard Music Award) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Billboard_Music_Awards] , the  [LINK: (BBC Sound Of...) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BBC_Sound_of...]  poll, 17  [LINK: (BMI London Awards) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BMI_awards] , a  [LINK: (Cannes Lions Award) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cannes_Lion_Awards] , two  [LINK: (Glamour Awards) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glamour_Awards] , a  [LINK: (Global Award) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Global_Awards] , an  [LINK: (iHeartRadio Music Award) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IHeartRadio_Music_Awards] , one  [LINK: (MTV Italian Music Award) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MTV_Italian_Music_Awards] , an  [LINK: (NRJ Music Award) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NRJ_Music_Award] , a  [LINK: (Q Award) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Q_Awards] , a  [LINK: (Teen Choice Award) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Teen_Choice_Awards]  and a  [LINK: (Variety Hitmakers Award) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Variety_Hitmakers_Awards] . [LINK: ([380]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-380]  Alongside those accolades, she has been nominated for numerous major music awards including, two  [LINK: (Grammy Award) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grammy_Awards]  nominations, a  [LINK: (Danish Music Award) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Danish_Music_Awards] , a  [LINK: (Latin American Music Award) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Latin_American_Music_Awards] , a  [LINK: (People's Choice Award) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/People%27s_Choice_Awards] , three  [LINK: (MTV Video Music Award) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MTV_Video_Music_Awards] , seven  [LINK: (Electronic Dance Music Awards) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electronic_Dance_Music_Awards] , six  [LINK: (MTV Europe Music Awards) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MTV_Europe_Music_Awards] , and ten  [LINK: (World Music Awards) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_Music_Awards] . [LINK: ([381]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-381]  [LINK: ([382]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-382]

She was honoured with the  [LINK: (Variety Hitmakers) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Variety_Hitmakers_Awards]  Decade Award, in 2019, after ten years of consistent work as a hitmaker, [LINK: ([383]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-383]  with Goulding stating: "It's probably the first time I've really been acknowledged for this work". [LINK: ([384]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-384]  In the same year, Goulding was awarded with an honorary  [LINK: (Doctor of Arts degree) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doctor_of_Arts]  at the  [LINK: (University of Kent) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/University_of_Kent]  in recognition of her contribution to music. [LINK: ([385]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-385]  [LINK: ([386]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-386]  [LINK: ([387]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-387]  Meanwhile, in recognition as a songwriter she was presented with the  [LINK: (BMI President's Award) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BMI_award]  at the 2022  [LINK: (BMI London Awards) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BMI_Film_%26_TV_Awards]  ceremony. [LINK: ([388]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-:0-388]  Goulding was awarded with 'The Praeses Elit Award' from  [LINK: (Trinity College Dublin) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trinity_College_Dublin] , which is given to those who have left an impact in their respective fields, in 2023. [LINK: ([389]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-389]

Throughout her music career, Goulding has attached several records to her name. In 2015, Goulding became the first artist to replace herself from the top spot on the  [LINK: (Dance/Mix Show Airplay) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dance/Mix_Show_Airplay]  chart, when " [LINK: (Love Me Like You Do) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Love_Me_like_You_Do] " dethroned " [LINK: (Outside) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Outside_(Calvin_Harris_song)] ". [LINK: ([390]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-390]  Goulding's "Love Me Like You Do" also broke the record for the most-streamed track in a week on Spotify, surpassing " [LINK: (Uptown Funk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uptown_Funk] ". [LINK: ([391]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-391]  [LINK: ([392]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-392]  In 2019, Goulding set the record for most song entries by a British female artist in the US after " [LINK: (Hate Me) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hate_Me_(Ellie_Goulding_and_Juice_Wrld_song)] " became her fourteen entry on the  [LINK: (Billboard Hot 100) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Billboard_Hot_100] . [LINK: ([393]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-393]   [LINK: (Billboard) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Billboard_(magazine)]  ranked her as  [LINK: (one of the most successful artists of the 2010s decade) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Billboard_Decade-End] . [LINK: ([394]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-394]  [LINK: ([395]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-395]  Billboard also ranked Goulding as the 62nd biggest female artist of the 21st century in March 2025. [LINK: ([396]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-396]  In the United Kingdom, Goulding has the most number-one albums by a British female artist (tied with  [LINK: (Adele) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adele] ), with four of her five studio albums ( [LINK: (Lights) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lights_(Ellie_Goulding_album)] ,  [LINK: (Halcyon) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Halcyon_(album)] ,  [LINK: (Brightest Blue) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brightest_Blue] , and  [LINK: (Higher Than Heaven) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Higher_Than_Heaven] ) topping the chart. [LINK: ([397]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-397]  Goulding's cover of  [LINK: (Joni Mitchell) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joni_Mitchell]  ' [LINK: (River) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/River_(Joni_Mitchell_song)] ' was the final number-one single of the 2010s in the United Kingdom. [LINK: ([398]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-398]  Goulding ranks as the third British female artist with most number-ones singles with four chart-topping singles: " [LINK: (Burn) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burn_(Ellie_Goulding_song)] " (2013), " [LINK: (Love Me Like You Do) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Love_Me_like_You_Do] " (2014), " [LINK: (River) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/River_(Joni_Mitchell_song)] " (2019) and " [LINK: (Miracle) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Miracle_(Calvin_Harris_and_Ellie_Goulding_song)] " (2023), just behind  [LINK: (Jess Glynne) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jess_Glynne]  and  [LINK: (Cheryl) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cheryl_(singer)] . Goulding currently holds the record for most song entries by a British female solo artist in the  [LINK: (UK Singles Chart) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/UK_singles_chart]  with 36 song entries, surpassing  [LINK: (Dame Shirley Bassey) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shirley_Bassey]  in 2023. [LINK: ([399]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-399]

For her support to the  [LINK: (LGBTQ+ community) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/LGBT_community] , Goulding has been honoured with the 'Ally Award' (2022) by the  [LINK: (Attitude Awards) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Attitude_(magazine)] , [LINK: ([400]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-400]  the 'Celebrity Ally' (2019) by  [LINK: (British LGBT Awards) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/British_LGBT_Awards] , and a nomination in the same category at the 2022 ceremony. [LINK: ([401]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-401]  [LINK: ([402]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-402]

For her constant  [LINK: (activism) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Activism]  on  [LINK: (climate change awareness) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Climate_change] , Goulding has received numerous recognitions, some of her honours include being awarded with the  [LINK: ('Global Leadership Award') -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Global_Leadership_Awards]  (2017) for her environmental and social justice activism, and being named 'Humanitarian of the Year' (2022) for her work raising the profile of fossil fuel-funded conflicts, including in  [LINK: (Ukraine) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ukraine] , and her support for refugees from conflict zones and the frontline of the climate crisis, both awards were given by the  [LINK: (United Nations Foundation) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_Nations_Foundation] . [LINK: ([328]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-:5-328]   Goulding was honoured at the  [LINK: (TIME 100 Impact Awards) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TIME100_Impact_Awards]  with the 'Impact Award' in recognition of her longstanding work toward advancing climate change awareness, in 2022. [LINK: ([403]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-403]  In 2024, Goulding was presented as the eleventh recipient of  [LINK: (The Perfect World Foundation Award) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Perfect_World_Foundation] , becoming the first musician to be recognised with 'The Conservationist of the Year' title, by the environmental organisation. [LINK: ([404]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-404]  [LINK: ([405]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-405]  She was also awarded with the 'Impact Award' by the  [LINK: (Playing For Change Foundation) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Playing_for_Change]  for her work as an artist and philanthropist, that same year. [LINK: ([310]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-:6-310]  In 2025, Goulding was appointed by  [LINK: (King Charles III) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_III]  as a  [LINK: (Member of the Order of the British Empire) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Member_of_the_Most_Excellent_Order_of_the_British_Empire]  (MBE) on the  [LINK: (2026 New Year Honours list) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_New_Year_Honours] , for her services to 'Biodiversity and the Climate'. [LINK: ([406]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-406]  [LINK: ([407]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-407]  [LINK: ([408]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-408]


