# IN POPULAR CULTURE #

Goulding's music contributions on visual media has been highlighted by both music and film critics. [LINK: ([412]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-412]  [LINK: ([413]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-413]  Her best-known collaborations include her song " [LINK: (Love Me Like You Do) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Love_Me_like_You_Do] " for  [LINK: (Fifty Shades of Grey) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fifty_Shades_of_Grey_(soundtrack)] , [LINK: ([414]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-414]  "Bittersweet" for  [LINK: (The Twilight Saga: Breaking Dawn – Part 2) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Twilight_Saga:_Breaking_Dawn_%E2%80%93_Part_2] , "Mirror" for  [LINK: (The Hunger Games: Catching Fire) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Hunger_Games:_Catching_Fire] , [LINK: ([415]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-415]  " [LINK: (Still Falling for You) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Still_Falling_for_You] " for  [LINK: (Bridget Jones's Baby) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bridget_Jones%27s_Baby:_Original_Motion_Picture_Soundtrack] , [LINK: ([416]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-416]  "Do You Remember" for  [LINK: (Fighting with My Family) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fighting_with_My_Family] ; " [LINK: (How Long Will I Love You) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/How_Long_Will_I_Love_You%3F] " for  [LINK: (About Time) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/About_Time_(2013_film)] , and the  [LINK: (Divergent) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Divergent_(film)]   [LINK: (soundtrack) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Divergent:_Original_Motion_Picture_Soundtrack] , including " [LINK: (Beating Heart) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beating_Heart_(Ellie_Goulding_song)] ". [LINK: ([417]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-417]  [LINK: ([418]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-418]  For television, Goulding has recorded original songs for the  [LINK: (HBO) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HBO]  series  [LINK: (Girls) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Girls_(TV_series)] , [LINK: ([419]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-419]  and  [LINK: (Game of Thrones) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Game_of_Thrones] , [LINK: ([420]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-420]  and collaborated with  [LINK: (Steve Price) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steve_Price_(musician)]  for the  [LINK: (Netflix) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Netflix]  original series  [LINK: (Our Planet) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Our_Planet] . [LINK: ([421]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-421]  For musicals, Goulding recorded a cover for the Broadway musical album,  [LINK: (Finding Neverland) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Finding_Neverland_(musical)] , [LINK: ([422]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-422]  and three original songs for the  [LINK: (Amazon) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amazon_(company)]  podcast series Crush Hour: A Musical. [LINK: ([423]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-423]

During the  [LINK: (2010s) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2010s_in_culture] , Goulding music was heavily used on films and television series, including  [LINK: (The Killing of a Sacred Deer) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Killing_of_a_Sacred_Deer] ,  [LINK: (Spring Breakers) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spring_Breakers_(Music_from_the_Motion_Picture)] ,  [LINK: (The Host) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Host_(2013_film)] ,  [LINK: (Now Is Good) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Now_Is_Good] ,  [LINK: (Marvel's Cloak & Dagger) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cloak_%26_Dagger_(TV_series)] ,  [LINK: (Teen Spirit) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Teen_Spirit_(2018_film)] ,  [LINK: (Cinderella) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cinderella_(2015_American_film)] ,  [LINK: (Glee) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glee_(TV_series)] ,  [LINK: (Arrow) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arrow_(TV_series)] ,  [LINK: (Teen Wolf) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Teen_Wolf_(2011_TV_series)] ,  [LINK: (Gossip Girl) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gossip_Girl] ,  [LINK: (Supergirl) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Supergirl_(TV_series)] , and  [LINK: (New Girl) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_Girl] . [LINK: ([424]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-424]  [LINK: ([425]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-425]  [LINK: ([426]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-426]  [LINK: ([427]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-427]  Goulding performed the theme song for American television network  [LINK: (The CW) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_CW] . Actresses  [LINK: (Elle Fanning) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elle_Fanning]  covered " [LINK: (Lights) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lights_(Ellie_Goulding_song)] " for the film  [LINK: (Teen Spirit) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Teen_Spirit_(soundtrack)] , [LINK: ([428]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-428]   [LINK: (Melissa Benoist) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Melissa_Benoist]  covered " [LINK: (Anything Could Happen) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anything_Could_Happen] " for the  [LINK: (fourteen episode) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/I_Do_(Glee)]  of the four season of  [LINK: (Glee) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glee_(TV_series)] , and  [LINK: (Raffey Cassidy) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raffey_Cassidy]  performed " [LINK: (Burn) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burn_(Ellie_Goulding_song)] " for the film  [LINK: (The Killing of a Sacred Deer) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Killing_of_a_Sacred_Deer] . [LINK: ([429]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-429]

According to  [LINK: (Billboard) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Billboard_(magazine)]  magazine, Goulding's music has been sampled numerous times on  [LINK: (Hip-Hop/Rap) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hip_hop_music]  music, among the most notable samples are: [LINK: ([430]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-:2-430]   [LINK: (Drake) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Drake_(musician)]  and  [LINK: (Jay-Z) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jay-Z] , " [LINK: (Pound Cake/Paris Morton Music 2) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pound_Cake_/_Paris_Morton_Music_2] " (2013) which samples Goulding's track 'Don't Say a Word' (2012); [LINK: ([431]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-431]   [LINK: (Big Sean) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Big_Sean] ,  [LINK: (Wiz Khalifa) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wiz_Khalifa]  and  [LINK: (Chiddy Bang) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chiddy_Bang] 's " [LINK: (High) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Finally_Famous_(Big_Sean_album)] " (2011) which samples " [LINK: (Fighter Plane) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Under_the_Sheets] " (2009);  [LINK: (Vic Mensa) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vic_Mensa]  &  [LINK: (Skrillex) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skrillex] , " [LINK: (No Chill) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/No_Chill] " (2016) which samples " [LINK: (Explosions) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Explosions_(song)] " (2012);  [LINK: (French Montana) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/French_Montana] 's " [LINK: (I Know) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CB5] " (2020) which samples " [LINK: (Starry Eyed) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Starry_Eyed_(Ellie_Goulding_song)] " (2010); [LINK: ([432]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-432]   [LINK: (Lil Baby) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lil_Baby] 's " [LINK: (In a Minute) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/In_a_Minute_(song)] " (2022) sampled "Don't Say a Word" (2012); [LINK: ([433]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-433]   [LINK: (Fivio Foreign) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fivio_Foreign] 's " [LINK: (World Watching) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_Watching] " (2022) sampled " [LINK: (Lights) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lights_(Ellie_Goulding_song)] " (2011);  [LINK: (Future) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Future_(rapper)]  and  [LINK: (Metro Boomin) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Metro_Boomin] 's " [LINK: (Mile High Memories) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mile_High_Memories] " (2023) which samples " [LINK: (Hanging On) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hanging_On_(Ellie_Goulding_song)] " (2012); and most recently  [LINK: (Fuerza Regida) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fuerza_Regida] 's " [LINK: (Tu Sancho) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tu_Sancho] " (2025) which samples "Don't Say a Word" (2012). [LINK: ([430]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-:2-430]  [LINK: ([434]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-434]

Portrayals in fiction

In 2016, Goulding was portrayed by actress Lizzy Connolly in  [LINK: (Channel 4) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Channel_4] 's  [LINK: (parody) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parody]  series of the  [LINK: (British royal family) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/British_royal_family] ,  [LINK: (The Windsors) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Windsors] . [LINK: ([435]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-435]  [LINK: ([436]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-436]

In 2024, English comedian and actress  [LINK: (Lucia Keskin) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lucia_Keskin]  portrayed a fictionalised version of Goulding on the first-season finale of  [LINK: (BBC Three) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BBC_Three]  comedy series,  [LINK: (Things You Should Have Done) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Things_You_Should_Have_Done] . [LINK: ([437]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-437]  [LINK: ([438]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding#cite_note-438]


